# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# Why this exists (T009): this repo runs with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF in the working tree on checkout. Several Compose
# services (kafka-init, and any future ones) bind-mount a .sh file straight
# from the Windows working tree into a Linux container and execute it with
# bash. A CRLF-terminated shebang line or CRLF-terminated `if`/loop lines
# breaks bash parsing (`$'\r': command not found` or worse, silent no-ops) —
# this is a classic Windows-host + Linux-container gotcha, not a hypothetical.
# Pinning eol=lf means the working-tree copy that gets bind-mounted is always
# LF, no matter what a developer's local Git config does.
*.sh text eol=lf
